  <section>
    <h2>What About Vapes, Edibles, and Concentrates?</h2>
    <p>The price tables above covered flower in detail. The other categories follow the same general pattern but with different value plays.</p>
    <h3>Vapes and Cartridges</h3>
    <p>Maine cartridge pricing is broadly similar to flower: mid-tier 510-thread cartridges run $40-55, value-tier $25-35, premium $60-80. The cheapest consistently advertised cartridge price in Maine is at Cannabis Cured and Cannabis Haven, where Curaleaf Select and Grassroots house cartridges frequently run $25-30 on rotation. For solventless vaporizer products (live rosin carts), expect to add $15-25 to those numbers.</p>
    <h3>Edibles</h3>
    <p>Edible pricing in Maine is competitive because the category is well-supplied. A 100mg pack of gummies runs $15-40 depending on brand and quality. Value operators (Cannabis Cured, Cannabis Haven) post $15-20 specials on rotating brands. Premium operator (HIGHLY Cannaco, Theory Wellness) house brands run $35-50 for comparable potency.</p>
    <h3>Concentrates</h3>
    <p>Concentrate pricing has the widest spread of any category. Hydrocarbon extracts (wax, shatter, badder) run $30-50 per gram at value operators and $70-110 at premium operators. Solventless (rosin, hash) runs $50-95 at value operators and $100-140 at premium operators. The cheapest consistently advertised gram of solventless in Maine is at HIGHLY Cannaco in Brunswick, where their house rosin frequently posts $50-60 on rotation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>
    <p>The cheapest dispensary in Maine is the one in your region with an active deal rotation that you can stack a loyalty discount on top of. For Aroostook buyers, that is HighNorth and Full Bloom. For central Maine buyers, Cannabis Haven and Cannamax. For Bangor, Cannabis Cured. For southern Maine, Theory Wellness's rotation in Kittery and the Schedule 1 house brand in Portland. Portland proper has fewer deep discount options, but the metropolitan convenience makes the metro premium worth it for many buyers.</p>
    <p>The structural drivers of Maine's pricing — vertical integration, 280E, and below-mature-market production volume — are not going away in 2026. Maine will continue to run 10-20% above Colorado and Oregon, and 10-20% below Massachusetts and New York. The store-level price gap within Maine is wider than the gap between Maine and other Northeast states, which means the realistic path to a lower price is operator shopping and discount stacking, not waiting for a market correction.</p>
    <p>For the operator-side economics, the <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-market">Maine cannabis market guide</a> covers the statewide sales, license, and tax data. For the curated list of which stores are worth the drive regardless of price, see the <a href="/blog/best-maine-dispensaries-2026">best Maine dispensaries in 2026</a>. Prices in this guide reflect a Q1-Q2 2026 snapshot; always verify current pricing directly with the operator before driving.</p>
  </section>

